   "source": [
    "Your primary goal is to meticulously analyze the provided research paper's title and summary. Based on this analysis, you are to accurately classify the paper by identifying its single main category and all relevant subcategories.\n",
    "You will be provided with specific input materials for each paper to perform this classification. These materials include the paper's title and summary, which is the specific text to be classified. You will also receive the TARGET_CATEGORIES List, which is the authoritative and exhaustive list of all permissible categories and subcategories. Accompanying this will be an explanation for each category, providing detailed descriptions to help you understand the scope of each category and subcategory within the TARGET_CATEGORIES List. Finally, a set of correct examples will be supplied, showing input papers and their correctly assigned categories; these demonstrate the expected output structure and the logical application of categories.\n",
    "The task involves several key steps. First, you must consult the provided resources thoroughly. This means you are to exclusively use the TARGET_CATEGORIES List and the explanation for each category for all your classification decisions. It is imperative that you do not infer or use categories that are outside of this provided list. Second, you need to identify the main category. From the TARGET_CATEGORIES List, determine the single, most fitting main_category that best encapsulates the core subject and primary focus of the paper. Third, after identifying the main category, you must select all applicable subcategories. To do this, review the TARGET_CATEGORIES List again and select all other categories and subcategories from this list that logically and comprehensively apply to the paper's content, as evidenced by its title and summary. Crucially, ensure that the main_category itself is included in this selection of applicable categories.\n",
    "Your findings must be presented in a specific format. You are required to output your classification as a single JSON object. This JSON object must adhere to a precise structure, containing exactly two keys. The first key is \"main_category\", which should have a string value representing the single primary category you identified in the task steps. The second key is \"categories\", which should have a string value consisting of a comma-separated list of all categories and subcategories you selected. This list must include the main_category and all other logically applicable categories from the TARGET_CATEGORIES List. Please ensure there are no leading or trailing spaces around the commas or the category names within this string.\n",
